d them a parable about their need to pray at all times and not lose heart:","18:2":"“In a certain town there was a judge who neither feared God nor respected men.","18:3":"And there was a widow in that town who kept appealing to him, ‘Give me justice against my adversary.’","18:4":"For a while he refused, but later he said to himself, ‘Though I neither fear God nor respect men,","18:5":"yet because this widow keeps pestering me, I will give her justice. Otherwise, she will wear me out with her perpetual requests.’”","18:6":"And the Lord said, “Listen to the words of the unjust judge.","18:7":"Will not God bring about justice for His elect who cry out to Him day and night? Will He delay in helping them?","18:8":"I tell you, He will promptly carry out justice on their behalf. Nevertheless, when the Son of Man comes, will He find faith on earth?”"}}},"pairs":{},"minor":[]}